# Opts in but does NOT pass `within_view=`. The cap contribution is nothing
# (the parent's cap stays unchanged), because an omitted `within_view`
# parses to PUBLIC, the identity of the intersection. `visibility` is set to
# keep the `package()` call non-trivial.
#
# Note the DEFAULT `within_view` for targets below is widened to PUBLIC by
# this call: `inherit = True` unions the parent's list with the omitted
# (PUBLIC) one. That is the footgun the cap closes -- see `outside_dep`.
package(
    inherit = True,
    visibility = ["PUBLIC"],
)

enforce_within_view_intersection()
